So my gaming experience this week:

&amp;#x200B;

Queue exceeds estimated time, requeue, does it again. Change to a specific game mode and get an *even longer* estimated queue time.

&amp;#x200B;

When it did pop, I was 2 stacks + me + 2 newbies versus 3 stacks + 2 stacks. Ok, so high level doesn't mean skill right? We just got stomped by coincidence.

&amp;#x200B;

Next game: triple warrior, Auriel, Chromie. Um ya... we got stomped even harder.

&amp;#x200B;

You might notice it's a sample size of 2 games, so despite it being pick none of the above I won't make that conclusion. However it's not for lack of trying, every other attempt to queue has taken ~5 minutes and I've given up to go play AI / Brawl / Ranked / Other Games.

Even when it's positive it's just a weird system.  I had a 3 game losing streak so my PRA went up a point since now I'm even further away from my target rank...  Then the game exploded during draft so I lost 600 points and my PRA jumped up again lol.

&amp;#x200B;

Other than this weirdness it doesn't mean anything though.  My favored adjustment each match is still very small (or non-existent).  So it's not like my mmr / rank mismatch is actually effecting anything.

Clicking the roulette is just cosmetic.  First iteration there were people who showed screenshots of it landing on something and getting something else.

&amp;#x200B;

As you can imagine, if the game crashed while roulette spun what would happen?  It has to give you a result even if you never clicked it.  So it's just cosmetic and your value is already computed once you pull up the roulette screen.

&amp;#x200B;

Your experience and other people who closed the game / crashed / whatever during roulette are all the same, so I'm pretty comfortable saying that's how it works.

